WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.200
Dave Bautista, you sneaky scoundrel, you.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.230
The Guardians of the Galaxy star has got DC
fans losing their minds over a photo he posted

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.469
to his Twitter account which seems to suggest
that he may be in talks to star in a film

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:15.400
produced by Warner Bros. DC's parent company.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.700
Stoking the fires of speculation even further,
Bautista provocatively captioned the image:

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.189
"It won't come to you so get after it!!

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.180
#DreamChaser"

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.720
Yeah, we'd say that's a pretty strong indication
that Bautista is actively pursuing a specific

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:29.220
role.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.720
Fans, of course, took that indication and
ran with it and there's a pretty strong consensus

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.060
among them as to just what role that might
be.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.680
Of course, Bautista is well-known for his
role as Drax the Destroyer in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.470
Universe, and it's also fairly common knowledge
that he was the first choice for the role

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:49.940
of Peacemaker in Guardians of the Galaxy director
James Gunn's upcoming DC picture The Suicide

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.460
Squad though that role eventually went to
fellow wrestler John Cena.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:58.170
Given this history, fans are convinced that
the actor is lobbying to secure a role in

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.400
writer/director Matt Reeves' upcoming The
Batman and with his build, it seems like he'd

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.900
be a pretty good fit to play Bane, the Bat-breaking
baddie who was previously portrayed in The

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.580
Dark Knight Rises by Tom Hardy.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.260
Virtually every response to Bautista's tweet
contained the words "Bane" and "Please."

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.360
Hey a little hope never hurt nobody!

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.760
"I learned here that there can be no true
despair without hope."

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.060
Look, if anybody can picture Bautista filling
Bane's shoes, it's us.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.800
It's not just his build; his voice, acting
style, and proven action chops would have

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.960
us totally flipping out it if he were to one
day land the role.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:38.940
Unfortunately, we're approximately 99.9998
percent sure that that day isn't going to

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.240
come today, next week, or next year.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.380
First and foremost, there's the fact that
The Batman's rogues' gallery is already pretty

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.340
well filled out.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:51.640
Back in October, Zoë Kravitz nabbed the role
of Catwoman; near-simultaneously, it was announced

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.620
that Paul Dano had been cast as the Riddler.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:57.780
The following month, the news broke that Colin
Farrell was in talks to play the Penguin in

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.670
the movie, and since then, it's also been
announced that John Turturro will be playing

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:04.120
the infamous crime boss Carmine Falcone.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.080
That's a pretty well-rounded gallery, and
even the rumors that have flitted about like

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.420
so many bats in a cave over the last year
or so have failed to mention Bane.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:16.830
It also stands to reason that assuming Warner
Bros. would like The Batman to kick off a

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.540
franchise, which is a pretty soundly reasonable
assumption — they're not going to load up

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.380
the plate with all of Bats' most iconic villains
right off the, er, bat?

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.600
I can't believe I just said that

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:32.360
The Joker, for instance, is conspicuously
missing from The Batman's villain lineup,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:36.450
and when it comes to truly threatening, formidable
Batman villains, there are virtually none

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:41.200
quite so threatening or formidable as Bane,
who famously snapped Bruce Wayne's back during

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.090
the events of the iconic DC story arc Knightfall.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.540
There's also the fact that Bautista is lined
up to be very, very busy for the foreseeable

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.060
future.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:54.040
He has no fewer than three projects in various
stages of pre-production, including Marvel's

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.040
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, director D.J.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.570
Caruso's crime thriller The Killer's Game,
and the animated... um, breakdancing mouse

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.840
flick Groove Tails.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:03.980
Yeah, we have no idea…

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.600
Of course, it's not outside the realm of possibility
that Bautista is reaching out to Warner Bros.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.660
in the event that Bane will appear in a sequel
to The Batman but it should be noted that

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.959
DC is being very cautious with its legacy
characters these days, having learned its

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.080
lesson from the failed universe-building attempt
of the early DCEU efforts.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.660
Star Robert Pattinson, who should know a thing
or two about whether he's signed on for a

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.989
film or a franchise, has deflected talk of
a sequel to The Batman so it seems pretty

00:03:28.989 --> 00:03:33.180
likely that Warner Bros. wants to gauge how
fans react to the flick before going ahead

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.840
and greenlighting more installments.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.300
That said, we can all hope.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.020
If Bautista does one day take on the role
of Bane, we have no doubt that he'll absolutely

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:45.160
kill it, most likely breaking the box office
along with the Bat.

